# Domain and Database

The canonical transcript is timestamped segments, not one giant string. VTT is an export artifact.

```ts
export interface TranscriptSegment {
  id: number;
  sequence: number;
  startMs: number;
  endMs: number;
  speaker?: string;
  text: string;
}
```

IDs are auto-increment integers (not UUIDs).

## Recordings

Statuses live on `RecordingStatus` in `@mintreels/schema` (`uploaded` | `processing` | `ready` | `failed`). Do not repeat those strings.

MySQL 8 (TypeORM in `packages/db`) stores metadata and object keys, never video binaries or embeddings. Validation + DTOs come from `@mintreels/schema` (zod + TypeScript enums); TypeORM entities align to zod `*RowSchema` shapes.

## TypeORM reads

Prefer `find` / `findOne` / `count` / `In` with relation `where` (e.g. `{ recording: { project: { userId } } }`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — QueryBuilder for a simple tenant read
this.createQueryBuilder('clip').innerJoin(Recording, 'recording', '...').getMany();

// ✅ GOOD
this.find({ where: { recording: { project: { userId } } }, relations: { recording: { project: true } } });
```

Do **not** hand-write QueryBuilder or raw SQL for tenant-scoped list/get. Add `@ManyToOne` / `@OneToMany` on existing FK columns so nested `where` works.

QueryBuilder is allowed only when `find` cannot express it. If the user-scoped row set is bounded, `find` then count/filter in memory instead of `SUM(CASE …)`.

## Repositories (one table)

Each `*Repository` queries **only its entity**. No `this.manager.find(OtherEntity)`. No methods that assemble rows from other tables.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — ProjectRepository loading clips/hooks/jobs
this.manager.find(Clip, { where: { recordingId: In(ids) } });

// ✅ GOOD — ClipRepository only
this.find({ where: { recordingId: In(ids) } });
```

Cross-table reads belong in `apps/api` services: inject each table's repository, call them, then combine.

Nested `where` / `relations` on **this** entity's FKs (e.g. `find({ where: { project: { userId } } })`) is allowed — that still returns this table's rows.

## Enums

Canonical values are TypeScript enums in `@mintreels/schema` (`packages/schema/src/enums.ts`). Zod schemas use those enum members. API and db code import the enum — never `'ready'`, `'failed'`, `'global'`, `'9:16'`, or env key strings inline.

## Knowledge bases

Scopes: `KnowledgeBaseScope.Recording` (one KB per recording) and `KnowledgeBaseScope.Global` (one project-wide KB).

Store `provider` and `provider_knowledge_base_id`. “Add to global KB” goes through `KnowledgeBaseProvider` — do not copy vectors into MySQL.

## Domain package

`packages/domain` holds product types and rules (`recordings`, `transcripts`, `summaries`, `hooks`, `clips`, `knowledge`, `jobs`). It must not import providers or vendor SDKs.
